#: ../../../../examples/tutorials/basics/text.py:1109
msgid ""
"<div class=\"sphx-glr-thumbcontainer\" tooltip=\"This pseudo-cylindrical, "
"equal-area projection was developed by the German mathematician and "
"astronomer Karl Brandan Mollweide in 1805. Parallels are unequally spaced "
"straight lines with the meridians being equally spaced elliptical arcs. The "
"scale is only true along latitudes 40°44&#x27; north and south. The "
"projection is used mainly for global maps showing data distributions. It is "
"occasionally referenced under the name homalographic projection.\">"
