#: ../../../../examples/tutorials/basics/text.py:1127
msgid ""
"<div class=\"sphx-glr-thumbcontainer\" tooltip=\"The Robinson projection, "
"presented by the American geographer and cartographer Arthur H. Robinson in "
"1963, is a modified cylindrical projection that is neither conformal nor "
"equal-area. Central meridian and all parallels are straight lines; other "
"meridians are curved. It uses lookup tables rather than analytic expressions "
"to make the world map &quot;look&quot; right [#f1]_. The scale is true along "
"latitudes 38° north and south. The projection was originally developed for "
"use by Rand McNally and is currently used by the National Geographic Society."
"\">"
